  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Phillips 66 has received $582M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Phillips 66 won 460 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $1.3M. Obligations fell 9.1% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a multi-year record of totals: FY21 $329M, FY22 $434M, FY23 $479M, FY24 $443M, FY25 $640M, FY26 $582M. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The award count and average award size together show that Phillips 66 is transacting through many mid-sized awards this fiscal year. The year-over-year decline of 9.1% contrasts with the FY25 total of $640M and the FY26 total so far of $582M. These figures are contract obligations except where tables list award values and expiring-contract totals as total contract values. This snapshot describes size, tempo, and recent change in Phillips 66 federal contracting activity without attributing future performance or causes for the change.",
